  42:     """Recolor each closed orthogonal line loop so convex bend pixels are yellow and concave bend pixels are red.
  43: 
  44:     Input structure
  45:     - The grid has a dominant background and exactly one foreground color.
  46:     - The foreground forms one or more 4-connected one-pixel-wide closed cycles; every foreground pixel has degree 2.
  47:     Rule
  48:     - Trace each cycle and inspect the turn at each foreground pixel.
  49:     - Straight pixels keep the original foreground color.
  50:     - Bend pixels whose turn direction is the majority direction for that cycle are convex corners and become yellow.
  51:     - Bend pixels whose turn direction is the minority direction for that cycle are concave corners and become red.
  52:     Key insight
  53:     - A simple rectilinear closed boundary has exactly four more convex bends than concave bends, so convexity can be inferred structurally from the majority turn sign within each traced cycle.
  54:     """
